{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/spectralordering(weight:normalized:tolerance:maxiterations:)-4odqr"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The spectral ordering (Barnard, Pothen and Simon): the components in order of their least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex index; a component of at most two vertices in index order; a larger one ascending by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the Fiedler vector of that component (for a connected graph, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fiedlerVector()"},{"text":"’s), entries","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"within 10⁻⁸ · max|x| of their predecessor kept in index order. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[]"},{"text":" for the empty graph.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"spectralOrdering","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = false, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-8, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","text":"NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"] ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryInteger","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sz","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepted when its residual is at most ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":"s (34 n from 5,000","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"solver.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Every weight is finite and nonnegative, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", when given, is at least 1.","type":"text"}]}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Throws","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the Lanczos run on L⁺ spends "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" matrix–vector"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"products (1,000 when nil) without converging, with the products spent and the Ritz"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"residual relative to 1\/λ₂. The run on σI − L that may come first hands over to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 + 20√n products or "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whichever is smaller. Each shift-invert product is a conjugate-gradient solve that throws,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with its own iterations and relative residual, after 20,000 + 2n. Below 64 vertices the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver answers and "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is unused. Only a tolerance below rounding has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached the default limits in the measurements."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"spectralOrdering"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"text":") -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentif